	(text "The Intellivision's cartridge port: 44 contacts, 2 x 22 at 2.54 mm.  Yannick's footprint numbers the fingers A1-A22\n(component face) and B1-B22 (back), left to right seen from the component face, contacts down: finger A(k) is INTV\npin 46 - 2k, B(k) pin 45 - 2k (even pins in front, odd behind); each pin is named with its INTV number.\nThe CP1610 bus (AD0-15, BDIR, BC1, BC2) and MSYNC reach the RP2354A straight (fujinet-firmware pico/intellivision\nboards/fujicard.h: MI_AD0_PIN 0, MSYNC 21, BDIR 22, BC1 26, BC2 27, RST 20).  GP26 / GP27 (BC1 / BC2) are ADC pins,\nnot 5 V tolerant (GP0-25 are), as on the PiNTY CARD.  GP20 high turns Q1 on: the console's /RESET (pin 12) low.\nGP28 drives EXT_AUDIO (pin 6, the ECS audio) through 1k (pintycard.h MI_AUDIO_PIN 28).  The three shorted pairs pass a\nconsole signal through the cart (32 / 42, 34 / 40, 36 / 38).  GP16 / GP17 go to the TX / RX pads."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 106.68 71.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c75d0086-5d92-56a3-afb6-21a3f76e0c56")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
